{title: Carpenter's Son}
{subtitle: Matthew 13:55–56; Mark 6:3; Matthew 27:56; Mark 15:47}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 79}
{time: 2/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] | ×10

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Standing in the synagogue hall
[Bb]They ask who he really is
Isn't he the carpenter
[Bb]Working with his hands [Ab]and skills
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
His moth[Eb/G]er is named Mary
Brothers James and [Ab]Si[Eb]mon too
Joseph and Judas are there
Sis[Bb]ters watching as he [Eb]grew [Ebmaj7/D]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Cm]Where did [Ab]this man [Eb]get all these [Bb]things
[Cm]The carpen[Ab]ter's son they [Bb]say
[Ab]Isn't this [Eb/G]the son of Mary
[Bb]Walking in our [Cm]everyday
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Cm] | [Cm] | [Cm] | [Cm] |
| [Cm] | [Eb] | [Eb] | [Eb] |
| [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
At the cross she stood nearby
Mother [Bb]of James and Jo[Eb]seph
Watching from a distance
[Bb]Holding her grief in her skull
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Cm]Where did this [Ab]man get [Eb]all these [Bb]things
[Cm]The carpen[Ab]ter's son they [Bb]say
[Ab]Isn't this the [Eb/G]son of Mary
Walk[Bb]ing in our ev[Cm]eryday
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Eb]She saw where he was laid
In [Bb]the tomb of the silent [Eb]grave
{end_of_verse}
